1. Definitions

"The Mod" means Everything RGB Profiles: its source code, compiled builds,
default profile files, images, documentation and every other file in this
repository or in a release of it, except the Third-Party Components listed in
section 6.

"Official Sources" means the Mod's own project pages on Modrinth and
CurseForge, and the releases page of its GitHub repository.

2. What you may do

a. Download the Mod from an Official Source and use it, including in videos,
   streams and screenshots, whether or not those are monetised.

b. Include the Mod in a modpack published anywhere, as long as the modpack
   does not contain or re-host the Mod's files and instead has them downloaded
   from an Official Source when the pack is installed. For example:
   - a modpack on Modrinth or CurseForge that uses the Mod's project page on
     that platform;
   - a packwiz (or similar) modpack, hosted on GitHub or anywhere else, whose
     entry for the Mod points to a download on an Official Source.
   Committing, bundling or mirroring the Mod's jar inside the modpack itself,
   or in the modpack's repository, counts as redistribution under section 3a.

c. Read and study the source code, change it, and build changed versions for
   your own personal use.

d. Fork the repository on GitHub in order to contribute changes back to the
   Mod through pull requests.

3. What you may not do without written permission from the copyright holders

a. Redistribute the Mod, in compiled or source form, changed or unchanged,
   except as section 2 allows. This includes uploading it to any website,
   launcher or file host other than the Official Sources.

b. Publish, share or distribute a changed version of the Mod, or any other
   work that copies a substantial part of its source code or files.

c. Sell the Mod, charge for access to it, or put it behind a paywall.

d. Present the Mod, or any part of it, as your own work, or misrepresent
   where it came from.

